FORM K-1.
IN THE MATTER OF: the-harrow.
OFF THE RECORD: a Turing machine. The Harrow executes sentences; here
OFF THE RECORD: the sentences are statements, which is the same thing.
OFF THE RECORD: The tape is two stacks of nested exhibits (the cons
OFF THE RECORD: cells of spec.md, section 18); the machine is the
OFF THE RECORD: two-state busy beaver, which halts after 6 sentences
OFF THE RECORD: with 4 marks on the tape. Its table:
OFF THE RECORD:   A,0 -> write 1, move right, B
OFF THE RECORD:   A,1 -> write 1, move left,  B
OFF THE RECORD:   B,0 -> write 1, move left,  A
OFF THE RECORD:   B,1 -> write 1, move right, halt
OFF THE RECORD: Every write is 1, so only direction and state vary.
OFF THE RECORD: A cell whose sym is -1 seals the bottom of a stack.

THE EXHIBIT OF cell, COMPRISING sym AND rest.

ARTICLE 1.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT left IS AN EXHIBIT OF cell WHEREIN sym IS -1 AND rest IS 0.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT right IS AN EXHIBIT OF cell WHEREIN sym IS -1 AND rest IS 0.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT state IS "A".
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT steps IS 0.

ARTICLE 2.
    OFF THE RECORD: one transition per visit. Read the head symbol.
    SHOULD state EQUAL "halt", REFER TO ARTICLE 6.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT head IS THE sym ENTERED IN right.
    SHOULD head EQUAL -1, LET IT BE RECORDED THAT head IS 0.
    FAILING WHICH, LET IT BE RECORDED THAT right IS THE rest ENTERED IN right.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT steps IS steps PLUS 1.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT dir IS "R".
    SHOULD state EQUAL "A" AND ALSO head EQUAL 1, LET IT BE RECORDED THAT dir IS "L".
    SHOULD state EQUAL "B" AND ALSO head EQUAL 0, LET IT BE RECORDED THAT dir IS "L".
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT nxt IS "A".
    SHOULD state EQUAL "A", LET IT BE RECORDED THAT nxt IS "B".
    SHOULD state EQUAL "B" AND ALSO head EQUAL 1, LET IT BE RECORDED THAT nxt IS "halt".
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT state IS nxt.
    SHOULD dir EQUAL "R", REFER TO ARTICLE 3.
    REFER TO ARTICLE 4.

ARTICLE 3.
    OFF THE RECORD: write 1 and move right: the written cell joins the
    OFF THE RECORD: left stack, and the head falls on the next right cell.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT left IS AN EXHIBIT OF cell WHEREIN sym IS 1 AND rest IS left.
    REFER TO ARTICLE 2.

ARTICLE 4.
    OFF THE RECORD: write 1 and move left: the written cell returns to
    OFF THE RECORD: the right stack, then the top of the left stack (or
    OFF THE RECORD: a fresh blank, if the tape must grow) becomes the head.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT right IS AN EXHIBIT OF cell WHEREIN sym IS 1 AND rest IS right.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT l IS THE sym ENTERED IN left.
    SHOULD l EQUAL -1, LET IT BE RECORDED THAT l IS 0.
    FAILING WHICH, LET IT BE RECORDED THAT left IS THE rest ENTERED IN left.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT right IS AN EXHIBIT OF cell WHEREIN sym IS l AND rest IS right.
    REFER TO ARTICLE 2.

ARTICLE 6.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT ones IS 0.

ARTICLE 7.
    OFF THE RECORD: the machine has halted; count the marks it left.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT s IS THE sym ENTERED IN right.
    SHOULD s EQUAL -1, REFER TO ARTICLE 8.
    SHOULD s EQUAL 1, LET IT BE RECORDED THAT ones IS ones PLUS 1.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT right IS THE rest ENTERED IN right.
    REFER TO ARTICLE 7.

ARTICLE 8.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT s IS THE sym ENTERED IN left.
    SHOULD s EQUAL -1, REFER TO ARTICLE 9.
    SHOULD s EQUAL 1, LET IT BE RECORDED THAT ones IS ones PLUS 1.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT left IS THE rest ENTERED IN left.
    REFER TO ARTICLE 8.

ARTICLE 9.
    PROCLAIM "The machine has halted after " PLUS THE TRANSCRIPT OF steps PLUS " sentences.".
    PROCLAIM "The tape bears " PLUS THE TRANSCRIPT OF ones PLUS " marks.".
    ADJOURN INDEFINITELY.
